Dockerfile Components
-------------------------------------------------------------
We can also call as KEYWORDS
All the components/keywords must be written in CAPITAL LETTERS

* FROM
* RUN
* CMD
* ENTRYPOINT
* COPY
* ADD
* WORKDIR
* LABEL
* ENV
* ARGS
* EXPOSE


1. FROM
From is used to Get the base image for our Container 

2.RUN 
* It is used to execute the command on top of base image 
* RUN Instruction will get executed while creating the image 
* we can right the multiple RUN 
* all RUN will be executed from top to bottom
* RUN is used to install any packages 

3. CMD
* It is used to excecute on top the base image 
* IT will be executed while creating the Container 
* We can write multiple CMD instruction But docker will only execute only the last CMD instruction .

4. COPY
* It isused to copy the file or folder to the docker image 
* It is used to copy the file from the one location to the other location 
* It is also used to copy the file from EC2 to Dockerfile 

COPY < SourceLocation> <Destination Location >

5. ADD 
* It is used to aad the file which is available on internet to the container 
* ADD command also used to download the filefrom internet 
* ADD keyword will extarct the tar file while copying the image .

6. WORKDIR
*  using this directory we can set the working directort of the image/container 
* It will help us to go inside the specified directory 

7. LABEL
* It isused to assgn the meta data for our image 
* LABELS are represent in the form of key:value pairs 
* Using lable we can Give the author name to the image

#To find the Author name 
----------------------------
docker inspect <containername> | grep -i <authorname>
(-i is for case sensitivity if not required you can remove the -i >

8. ENV
* It is used to set the environment varaible 
* ENV variable wil run inside the container 
* Here also we will go with the Key:Value pairs 


9. EXPOSE 
----------
* It is used to expose our application on a specific port number 

Lets say i have a GitHub repo, which has a sample html file. Now we need to write a Dockerfile to install apache webserver (to host the html page)

vi Dockerfile
FROM ubuntu
RUN apt update -y
RUN apt install apache2 -y
RUN apt install apache2-utils -y
RUN apt clean
RUN git clone <Giturl>
COPY ECR-ECS-Project/ /var/www/html/
RUN service apache2 restart
EXPOSE 80
CMD ["/usr/sbin/apachectl", "-D", "FOREGROUND"]
(Default path to run the application in foreground)



