DOCKER VOLUME
-------------------
* Volume Indicates storage 
* It is just a folder , inside the container 
* docker volume is to store the data of the docker containers 
* Aslo called as persistence volume 
*  we can share the docker volume from one container to the another container 
* One volume can be attached to a multiple container but , at a time we can attach to one volume to one container 
* We can create more than one volume to container 
* The data inside the volume will stored in local machine which is your instance 

Method  1 --Creating volume usiong Dockerfile 
-----------------------------------------------
vi Dockerfile 
FROM ubuntu
VOLUME ["volume 1"]

The Volume you have created will be stored in the EC2 instance also , to check that come out of the container and 
* cd /var/lib/docker/
do ls --> you will find the volume inside the file 
go inside of it you will find the lengthy file ---> cd ----> _data ----> ls ---> All your  file will be there 

* To see the volumes in the 
------------ docker volume ls --------------


Method 2 --
------------------
To Get the volume from one container to another container 
docker run -it --name <newcontainername> --volumes-from  <exixtingcontainer> <Baseimage>

